Role of Context Classes
Each context class encapsulates values that can be passed down to child React jsx components. In our program, we have the
following context classes: [DeviceContext, ThemeContext].

DeviceContext - Encapsulates the methods and state variables associated with the IBDC device. Device
context exposes:
 - State variables for the connected device
 - Methods for handling Bluetooth Low Energy connection

ThemeContext - Encapsulates top-level user interface style values that are passed down to each component specified
in the module. These styles applied at the top level and passed to the jsx children components ensure a consistent UI
throughout the application.


